e: ['91776-1791', '95035-4849', '92503-4925']\nState: The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Value of this column must in: ['CA']\nMailStreet:  The values' format are The unabbreviated mailing address of the school, district, or administrative authority. Note: 1) Some entities (primarily closed or retired schools) may not have data in this field; 2) Many active ent. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['6420 Rustic Lane', '4215 East Gleason Street', '3276 Cortona Drive']\nMailStrAbr:  The values' format are the abbreviated mailing street address of the school, district, or administrative authority.Note: Many active entities have not provided a mailing street address. For your convenience we have filled t. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['14935 Valerio St.', 'PO Box 687 PO Box 687', '6949 Genesee Ave.']\nMailCity:  The values' format are The city associated with the mailing address of the school, district, or administrative authority. Note: Many entities have not provided a mailing address city. For your convenience we have filled the. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Montebello', 'Whiskeytown', 'San Fracisco']\nMailZip:  The values' format are The zip code associated with the mailing address of the school, district, or administrative authority. Note: Many entities have not provided a mailing address zip code. For your convenience we have fi. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['96002-9210', '93024-0878', '90755-5858']\nMailState:  The values' format are The state within the mailing address. For your convenience we have filled the unpopulated MailState cells with State data.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Value of this column must in: ['CA']\nPhone: The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['(530) 824-7715', '(714) 527-8821', '(619) 388-1234']\nExt:  The column is The phone number extension of the school, district, or administrative authority.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [39117, 8110, 47499]\nWebsite:  The column is The website address of the school, district, or administrative authority.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['http://kordyak-rialto-ca.schoolloop.com/', 'www.fillmoreusd.org/', 'www.humboldt.k12.ca.us/hydesville_sd']\nOpenDate:  The column is The date the school opened.. The type is DATE, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['1990-11-26', '1974-08-01', '2009-09-08']\nClosedDate:  The column is The date the school closed.. The type is DATE, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['1990-05-07', '2003-06-06', '2011-08-02']\nCharter:  The column is This field identifies a charter school. .  The values' format are The field is coded as follows: · 1 = The school is a charter · 0 = The school is not a charter. The type is INTEGER, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Value of this column must in: [1, 0]\nCharterNum:  The column is The charter school number,.  The values' format are 4-digit number assigned to a charter school.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [1073, 928, 1254]\nFundingType:  The column is Indicates the charter school funding type.  The values' format are Values are as follows: · Not in CS (California School) funding model · Locally funded · Directly funded. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Not in CS funding model', 'Directly funded', 'Locally funded']\nDOC:  The column is District Ownership Code.  The values' format are The District Ownership Code (DOC) is the numeric code used to identify the category of the Administrative Authority. • 00 - County Office of Education • 02 – State Board of Education • 03 – Statewide . The type is TEXT, Which does not inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [56, 2, 54]\nDOCType:  The column is The District Ownership Code Type is the text description of the DOC category..  The values' format are (See text values in DOC field description above). The type is TEXT, Which does not inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Statewide Benefit Charter', 'Administration Only', 'County Office of Education (COE)']\nSOC:  The column is The School Ownership Code is a numeric code used to identify the type of school..  The values' format are • 08 - Preschool • 09 – Special Education Schools (Public) • 11 – Youth Authority Facilities (CEA) • 13 – Opportunity Schools • 14 – Juvenile Court Schools • 15 – Other County or District Programs • 3. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [62, 65, 14]\nSOCType:  The column is The School Ownership Code Type is the text description of the type of school.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Junior High Schools (Public)', 'Youth Authority Facilities', 'Continuation High Schools']\nEdOpsCode:  The column is The Education Option Code is a short text description of the type of education offered..  The values' format are  • ALTSOC – Alternative School of Choice • COMM – County Community School • COMMDAY – Community Day School • CON – Continuation School • JUV – Juvenile Court School • OPP – Opportunity School • YTH – . The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['TRAD', 'ALTSOC', 'SPEC']\nEdOpsName:  The column is Educational Option Name.  The values' format are The Educational Option Name is the long text description of the type of education being offered.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['County Community School', 'State Special School', 'Special Education School']\nEILCode:  The column is The Educational Instruction Level Code is a short text description of the institution's type relative to the grade range served..  The values' format are • A – Adult • ELEM – Elementary • ELEMHIGH – Elementary-High Combination • HS – High School • INTMIDJR – Intermediate/Middle/Junior High • PS – Preschool • UG – Ungraded. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['INTMIDJR', 'ELEMHIGH', 'A']\nEILName:  The column is The Educational Instruction Level Name is the long text description of the institution’s type relative to the grade range served.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Elementary', 'Intermediate/Middle/Junior High', 'Preschool']\nGSoffered:  The column is The grade span offered is the lowest grade and the highest grade offered or supported by the school, district, or administrative authority. This field might differ from the grade span served as report.  The values' format are For example XYZ School might display the following data: GSoffered = P–Adult GSserved = K–12. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['3-6', '1-6', 4]\nGSserved:  The column is It is the lowest grade and the highest grade of student enrollment as reported in the most recent certified CALPADS Fall 1 data collection. Only K–12 enrollment is reported through CALPADS. This field.  The values' format are commonsense evidence: 1. Only K–12 enrollment is reported through CALPADS 2. Note: Special programs at independent study, alternative education, and special education schools will often exceed the typ. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['K-12', 10, '7-11']\nVirtual:  The column is This field identifies the type of virtual instruction offered by the school. Virtual instruction is instruction in which students and teachers are separated by time and/or location, and interaction oc.  The values' format are The field is coded as follows: · F = Exclusively Virtual – The school has no physical building where students meet with each other or with teachers, all instruction is virtual. · V = Primarily Virtual. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['N', 'F', 'P']\nMagnet:  The column is This field identifies whether a school is a magnet school and/or provides a magnet program. .  The values' format are The field is coded as follows: · 1 = Magnet - The school is a magnet school and/or offers a magnet program. · 0 = Not Magnet - The school is not a magnet school and/or does not offer a magnet program.. The type is INTEGER, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Value of this column must in: [0, 1]\nLatitude:  The column is The angular distance (expressed in degrees) between the location of the school, district, or administrative authority and the equator measured north to south.. The type is REAL, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [34, 33, 38]\nLongitude:  The column is The angular distance (expressed in degrees) between the location of the school, district, or administrative authority and the prime meridian (Greenwich, England) measured from west to east.. The type is REAL, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [-122, -122, -118]\nAdmFName1:  The column is administrator's first name.  The values' format are The superintendent’s or principal’s first name. commonsense evidence: Only active and pending districts and schools will display administrator information, if applicable.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Coleen', 'Cammie', 'Randa']\nAdmLName1:  The column is administrator's last name.  The values' format are The superintendent’s or principal’s last name. commonsense evidence: Only active and pending districts and schools will display administrator information, if applicable.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Noblett', 'Vonstriver', 'Astor']\nAdmEmail1:  The column is administrator's email address.  The values' format are The superintendent’s or principal’s email address. commonsense evidence: Only active and pending districts and schools will display administrator information, if applicable.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['tsuanico@sandi.net', 'kevin.covert@tulare.k12.ca.us', 'mcalvero@vusd.org']\nAdmFName2:  The values' format are SAME as 1. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Philip', 'Steve', 'Alejo']\nAdmLName2: The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Ohle', 'Trombley', 'Chavez']\nAdmEmail2: The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['tdacosta@rcsdk8.net', 'mgrijalva@dpol.net', 's.benn@myebca.com']\nAdmFName3:  The values' format are not useful. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Michelle', 'Melissa', 'Amos']\nAdmLName3:  The values' format are not useful. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Gonzalez', 'Rivera', 'DeBoer']\nAdmEmail3:  The values' format are not useful. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['lydia.burgos@cvesd.org', 'roulette.mark@tusd.org', 'llamb@lcer.org']\nLastUpdate:  The values' format are when is this record updated last time. The type is DATE, Which does not inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['2015-12-17', '2000-06-19', '2016-02-22']\n\n#Forigen keys:\nfrpm.CDSCode = schools.CDSCode, satscores.cds = schools.CDSCode\n\n#Database Description:  \nThe database contains comprehensive information about schools in California, including demographic data, academic performance, meal eligibility statistics, and institutional characteristics. It integrates data from multiple sources to provide insights into school enrollment, student socioeconomic status (via free and reduced-price meal programs), SAT performance, geographic location, administrative details, and operational status. The data is structured across three interconnected tables linked by school identification codes, enabling analysis at both the institutional and regional levels.\n\n#Tables Descriptions:  \n**frpm**: Contains data related to Free and Reduced-Price Meal (FRPM) eligibility for California schools, serving as a proxy for student socioeconomic status. Includes enrollment figures, counts of students eligible for free or FRPM meals, and corresponding percentages for K–12 and ages 5–17 groups. Also includes school-level identifiers such as CDS code, district and county names, charter status, grade range, and certification status from CALPADS. All records are from the 2014–2015 academic year.\n\n**satscores**: Provides SAT performance metrics for schools in California, including the number of test takers, average scores in Reading, Math, and Writing, and the count of students achieving total SAT scores of 1500 or higher. Linked to schools via CDS code, it also includes enrollment data for grades 1–12 and geographic identifiers such as county, district, and school name.\n\n**schools**: Offers detailed institutional and geographic information about California schools, including physical and mailing addresses, contact details, administrator names and emails, charter status, funding type, ownership codes (district and school level), educational options, instructional levels, grade spans offered and served, virtual instruction type, and coordinates (latitude and longitude). It also tracks operational status through open and close dates and was last updated in 2015.\n", 'db_col_dic': {'frpm.CDSCode': ['The type is TEXT, Which does not inlude Null and is Unique. Values format like: [19647256057798, 37683386039978, 1612596001655]', '', '', 'TEXT', 'Non-Null', 'Unique', '[19647256057798, 37683386039978, 1612596001655]'], 'frpm.`Academic Year`': ["The type is TEXT, Which does not inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Value of this column must in: ['2014-2015']", '', '', 'TEXT', 'Non-Null', 'Non-Unique', "['2014-2