 inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['1990-05-07', '2003-06-06', '2011-08-02']", 'The date the school closed.', '', 'DATE', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['1990-05-07', '2003-06-06', '2011-08-02']"], 'schools.Charter': [" The column is This field identifies a charter school. .  The values' format are The field is coded as follows: · 1 = The school is a charter · 0 = The school is not a charter. The type is INTEGER, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Value of this column must in: [1, 0]", 'This field identifies a charter school. ', 'The field is coded as follows: · 1 = The school is a charter · 0 = The school is not a charter', 'INTEGER', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', '[1, 0]'], 'schools.CharterNum': [" The column is The charter school number,.  The values' format are 4-digit number assigned to a charter school.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [1073, 928, 1254]", 'The charter school number,', '4-digit number assigned to a charter school.', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', '[1073, 928, 1254]'], 'schools.FundingType': [" The column is Indicates the charter school funding type.  The values' format are Values are as follows: · Not in CS (California School) funding model · Locally funded · Directly funded. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Not in CS funding model', 'Directly funded', 'Locally funded']", 'Indicates the charter school funding type', 'Values are as follows: · Not in CS (California School) funding model · Locally funded · Directly funded', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['Not in CS funding model', 'Directly funded', 'Locally funded']"], 'schools.DOC': [" The column is District Ownership Code.  The values' format are The District Ownership Code (DOC) is the numeric code used to identify the category of the Administrative Authority. • 00 - County Office of Education • 02 – State Board of Education • 03 – Statewide . The type is TEXT, Which does not inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [56, 2, 54]", 'District Ownership Code', 'The District Ownership Code (DOC) is the numeric code used to identify the category of the Administrative Authority. • 00 - County Office of Education • 02 – State Board of Education • 03 – Statewide ', 'TEXT', 'Non-Null', 'Non-Unique', '[56, 2, 54]'], 'schools.DOCType': [" The column is The District Ownership Code Type is the text description of the DOC category..  The values' format are (See text values in DOC field description above). The type is TEXT, Which does not inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Statewide Benefit Charter', 'Administration Only', 'County Office of Education (COE)']", 'The District Ownership Code Type is the text description of the DOC category.', '(See text values in DOC field description above)', 'TEXT', 'Non-Null', 'Non-Unique', "['Statewide Benefit Charter', 'Administration Only', 'County Office of Education (COE)']"], 'schools.SOC': [" The column is The School Ownership Code is a numeric code used to identify the type of school..  The values' format are • 08 - Preschool • 09 – Special Education Schools (Public) • 11 – Youth Authority Facilities (CEA) • 13 – Opportunity Schools • 14 – Juvenile Court Schools • 15 – Other County or District Programs • 3. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [62, 65, 14]", 'The School Ownership Code is a numeric code used to identify the type of school.', '• 08 - Preschool • 09 – Special Education Schools (Public) • 11 – Youth Authority Facilities (CEA) • 13 – Opportunity Schools • 14 – Juvenile Court Schools • 15 – Other County or District Programs • 3', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', '[62, 65, 14]'], 'schools.SOCType': [" The column is The School Ownership Code Type is the text description of the type of school.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Junior High Schools (Public)', 'Youth Authority Facilities', 'Continuation High Schools']", 'The School Ownership Code Type is the text description of the type of school.', '', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['Junior High Schools (Public)', 'Youth Authority Facilities', 'Continuation High Schools']"], 'schools.EdOpsCode': [" The column is The Education Option Code is a short text description of the type of education offered..  The values' format are  • ALTSOC – Alternative School of Choice • COMM – County Community School • COMMDAY – Community Day School • CON – Continuation School • JUV – Juvenile Court School • OPP – Opportunity School • YTH – . The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['TRAD', 'ALTSOC', 'SPEC']", 'The Education Option Code is a short text description of the type of education offered.', ' • ALTSOC – Alternative School of Choice • COMM – County Community School • COMMDAY – Community Day School • CON – Continuation School • JUV – Juvenile Court School • OPP – Opportunity School • YTH – ', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['TRAD', 'ALTSOC', 'SPEC']"], 'schools.EdOpsName': [" The column is Educational Option Name.  The values' format are The Educational Option Name is the long text description of the type of education being offered.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['County Community School', 'State Special School', 'Special Education School']", 'Educational Option Name', 'The Educational Option Name is the long text description of the type of education being offered.', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['County Community School', 'State Special School', 'Special Education School']"], 'schools.EILCode': [" The column is The Educational Instruction Level Code is a short text description of the institution's type relative to the grade range served..  The values' format are • A – Adult • ELEM – Elementary • ELEMHIGH – Elementary-High Combination • HS – High School • INTMIDJR – Intermediate/Middle/Junior High • PS – Preschool • UG – Ungraded. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['INTMIDJR', 'ELEMHIGH', 'A']", "The Educational Instruction Level Code is a short text description of the institution's type relative to the grade range served.", '• A – Adult • ELEM – Elementary • ELEMHIGH – Elementary-High Combination • HS – High School • INTMIDJR – Intermediate/Middle/Junior High • PS – Preschool • UG – Ungraded', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['INTMIDJR', 'ELEMHIGH', 'A']"], 'schools.EILName': [" The column is The Educational Instruction Level Name is the long text description of the institution’s type relative to the grade range served.. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['Elementary', 'Intermediate/Middle/Junior High', 'Preschool']", 'The Educational Instruction Level Name is the long text description of the institution’s type relative to the grade range served.', '', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['Elementary', 'Intermediate/Middle/Junior High', 'Preschool']"], 'schools.GSoffered': [" The column is The grade span offered is the lowest grade and the highest grade offered or supported by the school, district, or administrative authority. This field might differ from the grade span served as report.  The values' format are For example XYZ School might display the following data: GSoffered = P–Adult GSserved = K–12. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['3-6', '1-6', 4]", 'The grade span offered is the lowest grade and the highest grade offered or supported by the school, district, or administrative authority. This field might differ from the grade span served as report', 'For example XYZ School might display the following data: GSoffered = P–Adult GSserved = K–12', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['3-6', '1-6', 4]"], 'schools.GSserved': [" The column is It is the lowest grade and the highest grade of student enrollment as reported in the most recent certified CALPADS Fall 1 data collection. Only K–12 enrollment is reported through CALPADS. This field.  The values' format are commonsense evidence: 1. Only K–12 enrollment is reported through CALPADS 2. Note: Special programs at independent study, alternative education, and special education schools will often exceed the typ. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['K-12', 10, '7-11']", 'It is the lowest grade and the highest grade of student enrollment as reported in the most recent certified CALPADS Fall 1 data collection. Only K–12 enrollment is reported through CALPADS. This field', 'commonsense evidence: 1. Only K–12 enrollment is reported through CALPADS 2. Note: Special programs at independent study, alternative education, and special education schools will often exceed the typ', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['K-12', 10, '7-11']"], 'schools.Virtual': [" The column is This field identifies the type of virtual instruction offered by the school. Virtual instruction is instruction in which students and teachers are separated by time and/or location, and interaction oc.  The values' format are The field is coded as follows: · F = Exclusively Virtual – The school has no physical building where students meet with each other or with teachers, all instruction is virtual. · V = Primarily Virtual. The type is TEXT, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: ['N', 'F', 'P']", 'This field identifies the type of virtual instruction offered by the school. Virtual instruction is instruction in which students and teachers are separated by time and/or location, and interaction oc', 'The field is coded as follows: · F = Exclusively Virtual – The school has no physical building where students meet with each other or with teachers, all instruction is virtual. · V = Primarily Virtual', 'TEXT', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', "['N', 'F', 'P']"], 'schools.Magnet': [" The column is This field identifies whether a school is a magnet school and/or provides a magnet program. .  The values' format are The field is coded as follows: · 1 = Magnet - The school is a magnet school and/or offers a magnet program. · 0 = Not Magnet - The school is not a magnet school and/or does not offer a magnet program.. The type is INTEGER, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Value of this column must in: [0, 1]", 'This field identifies whether a school is a magnet school and/or provides a magnet program. ', 'The field is coded as follows: · 1 = Magnet - The school is a magnet school and/or offers a magnet program. · 0 = Not Magnet - The school is not a magnet school and/or does not offer a magnet program.', 'INTEGER', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', '[0, 1]'], 'schools.Latitude': [' The column is The angular distance (expressed in degrees) between the location of the school, district, or administrative authority and the equator measured north to south.. The type is REAL, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [34, 33, 38]', 'The angular distance (expressed in degrees) between the location of the school, district, or administrative authority and the equator measured north to south.', '', 'REAL', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', '[34, 33, 38]'], 'schools.Longitude': [' The column is The angular distance (expressed in degrees) between the location of the school, district, or administrative authority and the prime meridian (Greenwich, England) measured from west to east.. The type is REAL, Which inlude Null and is Non-Unique. Values format like: [-122, -122, -118]', 'The angular distance (expressed in degrees) between the location of the school, district, or administrative authority and the prime meridian (Greenwich, England) measured from west to east.', '', 'REAL', 'Include Null', 'Non-Unique', '[-122, -122, -118]'], 'schools.AdmFName1': [" The column is administrator's first name.  The values' format are The superintendent’s or principal’s first name. commonsense evidence: Only active and pe